cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below. Problem statements and answers remain copyright of their respective competition organizers."
title: "Integration Bee Benchmark: Base Set (100) + Hard Set (100) with official answers"
abstract: >-
  A two-part benchmark of integration problems from real integration bees. Base Set: 100 problems
  from the MIT Integration Bee 2023/2024/2025 qualifying exams, UK University Integration Bee
  2025/26 Round 1, and the University of Florida Integration Bee 2025 written exam. Hard Set: 100 problems from knockout rounds of seven competitions (MIT Finals and
  Semifinals 2022-2026, Singapore Precollegiate IB 2026 Round 2, Lisbon 2025, UKUIB Round 3
  2024/25, Chulalongkorn 2025, Caltech 2025, Bonn 2026). Every answer is taken from the
  competition's own official answer key; every statement was transcribed from the official paper
  and screened for consistency with its answer.
authors:
  - alias: "Integration Bee Benchmark contributors"
version: "2.0"
date-released: "2026-09-08"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/orangeofcarl0-sys/integration-bee-benchmark"
keywords:
  - integration
  - benchmark
  - llm-evaluation
  - mathematics
  - integration bee
